[I] Universal Scene Description

[T] OpenUSD (Universal Scene Description) is a framework originally
[T] developed by Pixar for the interchange and composition of 3D computer
[T] graphics scene data. It provides C++ libraries, Python bindings and
[T] tools for authoring, reading and layering USD files.

[U] https://github.com/PixarAnimationStudios/OpenUSD

[A] PixarAnimationStudios
[M] andrei32 <andrei32.t2@gmai.com>

[C] extra/tool
[F] CROSS OBJDIR

# APL like
[L] Custom
[V] 26.11.1

[D] a9a862d1a824d24d2f967bf74eb8da83730d0184adb7b8ac0e6bd5bd OpenUSD-26.11.1.tar.gz https://github.com/PixarAnimationStudios/OpenUSD/archive/v26.11.1/

var_append GCC_WRAPPER_APPEND ' ' "-I$(pkgprefix includedir xorgproto) -L$(pkgprefix libdir xorgproto)"

var_append cmakeopt ' ' -DPXR_BUILD_TESTS=OFF
pkginstalled pyside6 || var_append cmakeopt ' ' -DPXR_BUILD_USDVIEW=OFF
